# Shell scripts must be stored and checked out with LF, always.
#
# Development happens on Windows, where core.autocrlf rewrites line endings on
# commit. A shell script committed with CRLF fails on Linux with the famously
# unhelpful `bash: \r: command not found` — the Render deploy and the Gradle
# wrapper both run on Linux, so this is a deploy-breaker rather than a cosmetic
# preference.
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
